  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Integration gap and provenance",
      "items": [
        "The shared pipeline writes raw uint32 token streams; training/pretrain.py:PretrainDataset reads shards with torch.load(weights_only=True). These formats do not interoperate today.",
        "160 \u00d7 50M-token shards \u224832 GB is budget arithmetic (8B \u00d7 4 bytes); actual shard inventory requires the packing manifest.",
        "Source revision 2edd9cdbf6b6708f103001c1d50fff2b05b32c85; the 55/20/25 grouping is a grouped view of the shared seven-source recipe."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Shared pipeline",
      "items": [
        "data/prepare_data.py is a shim over LLM/shared_data",
        "Only the tokenizer differs per project \u2014 shards stay comparable",
        "Mixture.yaml is authoritative: 8.0B tokens, weights sum to 1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Crash isolation",
      "items": [
        "Each stage runs as its own subprocess with per-source state files",
        "Shards are written tmp \u2192 fsync \u2192 os.replace, never torn",
        "The manifest is rebuilt from the shard files actually on disk",
        "manifest.json records SHA-256, provenance, and per-source stats"
      ]
    }
  ]
